    "final_assistant_text": "Done. I added the inverted-bounds guard to `clamp` in `src/mathkit/ranges.py`:\n\n```python\ndef clamp(value: int, lower: int, upper: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return ``value`` limited to the inclusive range ``[lower, upper]``.\"\"\"\n    if lower > upper:\n        raise ValueError(\"lower must not exceed upper\")\n    if value < lower:\n        return lower\n    if value > upper:\n        return upper\n    return value\n```\n\nThe change is exactly two new lines, comes before any clamping, and leaves `midpoint` and everything under `tests/` untouched. The full suite passes:\n\n```\nPYTHONPATH=src python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -t tests\n.... (Ran 4 tests) OK\n```\n\nAs a sanity check of the new behaviour: `clamp(5, 10, 0)` now raises `ValueError(\"lower must not exceed upper\")` instead of returning `10`, while all previous well-ordered behaviour is preserved.",
